## 🏗️ Build for production

```bash
npm run build
```

## 🐳 Docker

Build and run the production image:

```bash
docker build -t {{ project_name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }} .
docker run -p 8080:8080 \
  -e BACKEND_URL=https://your-api.example.com \
  {{ project_name | lower | replace(' ', '-') }}
```

The container uses `envsubst` to inject runtime environment variables into `env.js` at startup.

## 📁 Project structure

```
src/
├── assets/                # Static assets (images, fonts, etc.)
├── client/                # Auto-generated from OpenAPI
├── components/            # Shared components
├── hooks/                 # Custom hooks
├── pages/
│   ├── index.tsx          # Page exports barrel
│   └── home/
│       ├── HomePage.tsx
│       └── components/
├── App.tsx                # Router setup
├── main.tsx               # App entry point
├── env.ts                 # Runtime environment variables
└── index.css              # Tailwind CSS v4 entry
public/
├── env.js                 # Local dev env values
└── env.template.js        # Template for envsubst in Docker
```

## 🔧 Available commands

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `npm run dev` | Start dev server on port 8080 |
| `npm run build` | Production build |
| `npm run lint` | Run ESLint |
| `npm run lint:fix` | ESLint with auto-fix |
| `npm run format` | Prettier format |
| `npm run generate-api` | Regenerate OpenAPI client |

